            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Routes: 10.1.0.0/16 via A (metric 1), 10.1.1.0/24 via B (metric 50), 0.0.0.0/0 via C. Where does a packet to 10.1.1.5 go?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**B**: the /24 is the longest matching prefix.",
                "Metric and table order are never consulted first."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A router learns 10.5.0.0/16 from OSPF (cost 20) and RIP (2 hops). Which route is installed?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**OSPF**: administrative distance 110 beats RIP's 120.",
                "Metrics only compare routes within one protocol."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Host A pings server B across routers. Requests arrive, but no reply ever returns. What do you check?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The **return route** from B's side back to A's subnet.",
                "Routes must exist in both directions."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
